    "11": {
      "note": "The Review \\| Explanation switch stays in the top line. Each shown or compared saved revision carries its own binding, time, isolated frame and trusted stale list, and a claim return selects its resolved Review block with the walked tree retained. Published categories and grades feed the one change-set model: a category’s declared scale orders drawn changed blocks with Priority ties and an Ungraded (n) group, while chips retain presenter-inference labels, reasons and stale marks. Before work exists, the planned page uses the product’s planned · no changes line, an intended notice and deterministic-only effect orders with inert packet bodies. A matching live no-work move renews deterministic reads; work-bearing moves present the watcher’s notice and explicit Update instead of waking an explainer.\n\nAnchor: `useSurfaceExplainer`",
